cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Psyche, please cite the archived report of its first stage."
title: "Psyche"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Caliskan
    given-names: Cagan
repository-code: "https://github.com/cagancaliskan/psyche"
url: "https://cagancaliskan.github.io/psyche/"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Psyche is an open research project that builds brain-inspired components in stages, with
  artificial general intelligence (AGI) as its long-term aim. Each stage is built test-first and
  kept as a citable artifact. Stage 1, a dependency-free Python memory-and-activation substrate,
  is the foundation; its development is paused and its report is archived with a DOI. Stage 2,
  spiking cognitive maps, is the active line: it asks whether a spiking network that learns only
  through local synaptic plasticity shows, on classic cognitive-map paradigms, the behaviours that
  an internal map would explain, and what that behaviour costs as an analytic estimate of synaptic
  operations. No stage 2 results are reported yet.
keywords:
  - brain-inspired computing
  - cognitive maps
  - spiking neural networks
  - local plasticity
  - spreading activation
  - adversarial testing
  - determinism
  - reproducibility
# No version or date-released is given: the repository has no tagged release yet.
